{
 "section_summary": "This section continues a restricted study of Japanese left-wing politics from 1946 into 1947. It examines attempts to form a popular front, the April 1946 election, negotiations over the Yoshida cabinet, and efforts to unify labor organizations. The final pages turn to divisions within the Sanbetsu and the Nippon Nōmin Kumiai; a routing slip and an envelope interrupt the study between its numbered pages 159 and 160.",
