   "about": "Continues the study through the 1946–47 cabinet crisis, labor disputes, and splits in labor and farmers' organizations.",
   "summary": "Sanbetsu's overtures to Sōdōmei and the electric power dispute lead into renewed pressure for a cabinet change. The study follows the failed December 1946 Diet dissolution motion, unsuccessful January 1947 coalition talks, and SCAP's prohibition of the planned February 1 general strike. It then examines the limited unity achieved through Zenrōren, dissent over Communist influence in Sanbetsu, and the opening of the contentious February 1947 Nippon Nōmin Kumiai convention.",
